```c
// Missing code to recover interrupts snatched by KVM
kvm_xirr = kvmppc_get_xics_latch();
```
Reason:
The absence of the code to handle interrupts latched by KVM means that when KVM snatches interrupts, they are not recovered, leading to potential loss of interrupts and the CPU being stuck with an elevated CPPR.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
kvm_xirr = kvmppc_get_xics_latch();
if (kvm_xirr)
    return kvm_xirr;
```
Reason:
These statements ensure that any interrupts latched by KVM are checked and returned first, allowing the system to recover from interrupts that would otherwise be lost, thus preventing the CPU from getting stuck in an elevated CPPR state.

